I understand that quite a few people think the current setup with
genocide scrolls in Vanilla is a little too abusable. However,
UnNethack's way of dealing with it seems to depower it too much.

My solution?

Keep the effects of cursed scrolls of genocide the same.

Make blessed scrolls only eliminate one species at a time (as
opposed to classes), as UnNethack currently has it.

For uncursed scrolls, the chance of success should rely on
the difference of levels between the character and the monster('s base
level). For every level the base monster is over the character, there
should be a 2-5% chance that the scroll doesn't work (and/or summons a
couple of the monsters in; not as many as a cursed scroll, of course).
However, if the scroll works than the species should be genocided from
the game, as it always was. 

This would crack down on players eliminating master mind flayers 
after getting lucky on dungeon level 2, for example, while allowing
the scrolls to still maintain a decent value for players. 


